comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T18:28:16.551Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: quality:context-eval now executes the shipped CLI retrieval evaluator against the committed tracker corpus, checks query count plus nDCG/MRR/precision/recall against a versioned baseline, and runs an impossible perfect-score negative control that must exit nonzero. The query set grew from four saturated single-relevance judgments to five queries including an 11-item judgment set with partial recall. Live metrics: nDCG 0.6223, MRR 0.55, precision 0.16, recall 0.8545; the non-saturated query recall is 0.2727. Gate claims are cross-checked against the enforced workflow registry."
  "2026-07-29T18:36:30.282Z","harness:codex","Verification context correction: removed the legacy direct eval linked command because pm test correctly supplies an empty schema sandbox and the committed golden query file is therefore absent. The enforced quality:context-eval link pins the version-controlled read-only corpus explicitly and passed, while the focused evaluator suite stays sandbox-safe."
  "2026-07-29T18:51:20.983Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/813 at implementation head c7ac2767e. The PR description links this canonical record and includes live retrieval metrics, executable negative control, exact coverage, installed-consumer, security, and PM validation evidence."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T18:28:17.848Z","harness:codex",Baseline updates are explicit via --update and retain a 0.02 metric margin; ordinary runs execute the built dist/cli.js with the repository tracker pinned through --pm-path and telemetry disabled for deterministic CI.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T18:28:18.904Z","harness:codex",A retrieval threshold is not a negative control when every query has one relevant item and recall is saturated. Multi-relevant judgments plus an executable impossible threshold prove the CLI failure path and make ranking regressions observable.
